Subject: [PATCH 25/63] hardcode mask for macos slirp networking

Summary:
# Motivation:
The net argument is empty for some reason. Let's set a default? @tcare set it here: D79088873
# Overview:
- hardcode slirp net mask and address

Test Plan:
```
 m out/host/darwin-x86/cvd-host_package.tar.gz -k &> ~/build.logs.txt
HOME=/Users/achong/n-16/out/host/darwin-x86 out/host/darwin-x86/bin/launch_cvd  \
--use-overlay=false --vm_manager=qemu_cli  --system_image_dir=/Users/achong/n-16/out/host/darwin-x86 \
--qemu_binary_dir=/Users/achong/qemu/build \
--enable_host_uwb=false -device_external_network=slirp \
--vhost_user_vsock --enable_audio=true
```

Rollback Plan:

Reviewers: tcare, #cuttlefish-cross-platform, benthomas, josephknox

Reviewed By: tcare

Subscribers: tcare, ryanyu, <internal-group>

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.intern.facebook.com/D80636879
---
 host/libs/vm_manager/qemu_manager.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/host/libs/vm_manager/qemu_manager.cpp b/host/libs/vm_manager/qemu_manager.cpp
index fdc152b6f..6135102ba 100644
--- a/host/libs/vm_manager/qemu_manager.cpp
+++ b/host/libs/vm_manager/qemu_manager.cpp
@@ -852,9 +852,15 @@ Result<std::vector<MonitorCommand>> QemuManager::StartCommands(
       break;
     case cuttlefish::ExternalNetworkMode::kSlirp: {
       has_network_devices = true;
+#ifndef __APPLE__
       const std::string net =
           fmt::format("{}/{}", instance.ril_ipaddr(), instance.ril_prefixlen());
       const std::string& host = instance.ril_gateway();
+#else
+      const std::string net =
+        fmt::format("{}/{}", "10.0.2.15", "24");
+      const std::string& host = "10.0.2.2";
+#endif
       qemu_cmd.AddParameter("-netdev");
       // TODO(schuffelen): `dns` needs to match the first `nameserver` in
       // `/etc/resolv.conf`. Implement something that generalizes beyond
